[size=5][b]Wardrobe UI Improvements[/b][/size]

A redesign of the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/6945]Equipment-EX[/url] wardrobe screen. Instead of one long list of slots, you get a body column showing what V is wearing, a drawer of item cards for the selected slot, hover try-on, a camera that follows the body area, and outfits laid out as a grid.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Body column[/b]: what V is wearing, grouped by HEAD, BODY, ARMS, LEGS and FEET. Click an item or a + to jump to that slot.
[*][b]Item drawer[/b]: area tabs, a slot list with item counts, and a grid of named item cards. Pick 4, 5, 6 or 7 cards per row. Your choice is saved with your game.
[*][b]Search[/b]: filters as you type, and the X clears it. While you search, each area tab shows how many items match, e.g. LEGS (8).
[*][b]Hover to try on[/b]: rest the cursor on a card for a moment and V wears it in the preview. Move away and the real look comes back. Click to equip.
[*][b]Camera follows the area[/b]: HEAD, BODY, ARMS, LEGS and FEET each frame that part of V.
[*][b]NEW tags[/b]: items V didn't own the last time you opened the wardrobe are marked NEW, and so are the slots and tabs that hold them. A tag clears once you hover over or equip the item.
[*][b]Mod packs[/b]: each card names the clothing mod its item comes from, and PACK filters the grid to one pack. You can also search by pack name. Packs are detected automatically.
[*][b]Outfits[/b]: a four-column grid with item icons, search and favourites. Each outfit shows the playtime it was created at, and SORT orders them A-Z, newest or oldest first. After you change a saved look, UPDATE saves the change and REVERT puts the outfit back.
[*][b]EQUIPPED[/b] shows just what V is wearing, and [b]NEW[/b] just the items tagged NEW.
[*][b]Every game language[/b]: the labels follow the game's language, and you can change any label with a small TweakXL file (instructions in the README).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 2.5
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4198]ArchiveXL[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4197]TweakXL[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/6945]Equipment-EX[/url]
[/list]
Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], for the two switches below.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with Vortex or Mod Organizer 2, or extract the archive into the game folder (the folder that holds [i]bin[/i], [i]archive[/i] and [i]r6[/i]). Open the wardrobe the same way you do with Equipment-EX.

[b]Uninstall[/b]: delete [i]r6/scripts/WardrobeTabs[/i] and [i]archive/pc/mod/WardrobeTabs.archive[/i].

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
With Mod Settings installed, [i]Settings > Mods > Wardrobe UI Improvements[/i] has two switches, both on by default:
[list]
[*][b]Preview items on hover[/b]
[*][b]Move camera to the selected area[/b]
[/list]
Changes apply the next time you open the wardrobe.

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Mouse and keyboard only for now. Controller navigation isn't there yet.
[*]Translations other than English are machine translations. Corrections are welcome: post them in the comments or send the file.
[*]Pack names come from item IDs. A pack the mod doesn't know shows as its ID prefix in capitals. If your favourite pack shows up under a cryptic name, tell me in the comments and I'll add its proper name.
[*]Favourites, the outfit you last wore, NEW tags and the column choice are stored in your save. Saves made with the mod keep a little unused data after you uninstall it. This is harmless.
[*]The mod hooks the wardrobe without replacing Equipment-EX's code, so Equipment-EX keeps working as usual. Your outfits are Equipment-EX's own outfits.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]
[b]1.0.3[/b]
[list]
[*]Fixed: with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/33527]VFocus[/url] installed, outfits in the first column of the outfits view and the left part of the slot sidebar could not be clicked (VFocus's area for moving V took the clicks).
[/list]
[b]1.0.2[/b]
[list]
[*]The mod's labels are translated into every language the game offers and follow the game's language setting. Any label can be changed with a small TweakXL file; the README explains how.
[*]New: [b]NEW[/b] button next to EQUIPPED shows only the items tagged NEW. Hovering a card still clears its tag, but the card stays listed until you switch the filter off.
[*]EQUIPPED ONLY is now called EQUIPPED. EQUIPPED and NEW switch each other off.
[*]The PACK button and the packs in its list get the yellow NEW dot when they hold new items.
[*]New: outfits show the playtime they were created at.
[*]New: [b]SORT[/b] in the outfits view orders outfits A-Z, newest first or oldest first. Favourites stay on top. Your choice is saved with your game.
[/list]
[b]1.0.1[/b]
[list]
[*]Fixed: the PACK list showed only the first 18 packs, so packs further down the alphabet couldn't be picked. The list now scrolls with the mouse wheel and shows every pack.
[*]Opening the PACK list scrolls to the pack you picked.
[*]Outfits are now four to a row and use the full width of the drawer.
[/list]
[b]1.0.0[/b]
[list]
[*]First release.
[/list]

